  "verbalization": "Neridienone A appears to have a shared target of SNU-387 across multiple paths, which in turn is targeted by various compounds, including 5-Hydroxy-6,8-Dimethoxy-2,3-Dimethylbenzo[G]Chromen-4-One and 5-Hydroxytryptophan monohydrate, dl-. All these compounds ultimately target VMRC-MELG, suggesting a potential pathway where Neridienone A may exert its effects through a common mechanism involving SNU-387. The evidence supports a link between Neridienone A and VMRC-MELG via SNU-387, which is a key intermediate in the targeting process. The integration of these paths implies that Neridienone A may act through a mechanism that involves modulating the activity of SNU-387, which in turn influences VMRC-MELG. The relationship is supported by the consistent targeting of SNU-387 across different compounds, suggesting a possible shared biological function or pathway.",
